@startuml
skinparam defaultFontName Monospaced
skinparam defaultFontSize 11

title Figure 3-31 : Stop At Block Gap Request is Not Accepted at the Last Block of the Write Transfer\nFigure 3-32 : Continue Write Transfer by Continue Request

concise "DAT line" as DAT
binary "Stop At Block Gap Request (Control)" as STOP
binary "Continue Request (Control)" as CONT
binary "Write Transfer Active (Status)" as WTA
binary "DAT Line Active (Status)" as DLA
binary "Block Gap Event (Interrupt)" as BGE
binary "Transfer Complete (Interrupt)" as TC

scale 1 as 60 pixels

@0
DAT is "Block N-2"
STOP is low
CONT is low
WTA is high
DLA is high
BGE is low
TC is low

@3
DAT is "Gap"

@4
DAT is "Block N-1"

@7
DAT is "Gap"
STOP is high

@8
DAT is "Last block"

@11
DAT is "Busy"

@14
DAT is "Idle"
STOP is low
WTA is low
DLA is low
TC is high

note bottom of STOP
  Stop At Block Gap Request set to 1 during last block transfer.
  Host Controller shall NOT accept and terminates transaction normally.
  Block Gap Event Interrupt is NOT generated.
  Driver shall clear Stop At Block Gap Request.
end note

@16
DAT is {-}

@18
DAT is "Block M"
STOP is low
CONT is low
WTA is high
DLA is high
BGE is low
TC is low

@21
DAT is "Gap"
STOP is high

@23
DAT is "Stopped"
WTA is low
DLA is low
BGE is high

@27
CONT is high

@28
DAT is "Block M+1"
CONT is low
WTA is high
DLA is high
BGE is low

@31
DAT is "Gap"

@33
DAT is "Last block"

@36
DAT is "Busy"

@39
DAT is "Idle"
WTA is low
DLA is low
TC is high

highlight 23 to 27 #LightYellow : Stopped State

note bottom of CONT
  To restart: set Continue Request to 1
  (Stop At Block Gap Request shall be set to 0)
  
  After accepting Continue Request:
  (1) Set DAT Line Active and Write Transfer Active Status
  (2) Continue Request is automatically cleared
  
  End of transfer:
  (1) Clear Write Transfer Active, no Block Gap Event
  (2) Clear DAT Line Active, generate Transfer Complete
end note

@enduml